.TE
.PP
For single\-frame messages (the common case), flags is typically
\f[B]0x00\f[R].
The CONTINUED and FINAL flags enable streaming large payloads across
multiple frames.
.SH Payload format
Unless the \f[B]BINARY\f[R] flag is set, the payload is a UTF\-8 encoded
JSON object.
The JSON schemas for each channel are documented in
\f[B]bash\-server\-json\-messages\f[R](5).
.SH AUTO\-DETECTION
The server supports automatic protocol version detection on each new
connection.
The algorithm examines the \f[B]first byte\f[R] received:
.PP
.TS
tab(@);
lw(27.1n) lw(42.9n).
T{
First byte
T}@T{
Protocol selected
T}
_
T{
0x00\-0x05
T}@T{
\f[B]v2 binary\f[R] (byte is a valid channel ID)
T}
T{
\f[B]{\f[R] (0x7B) or *** (0x0A)
T}@T{
\f[B]v2 NDJSON\f[R] (see \f[B]bash\-server\-ndjson\f[R](5))
T}
T{
Any other printable ASCII
T}@T{
\f[B]v1 text\f[R] (see \f[B]bash\-server\-v1\-protocol\f[R](5))
T}
.TE
.PP
The first byte is consumed as part of the first message and is not
discarded.
Auto\-detection occurs exactly once per connection; the protocol cannot
be changed mid\-session.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SH Binary frame: AUTH message on CHAN_CONTROL
JSON payload:
\f[CR]{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqauth\(dq,\(dqtoken\(dq:\(dqa3f7...0e46\(dq}\f[R]
.PP
Assuming the payload is 78 bytes:
.IP
.EX
Offset  Hex
00      00              channel = 0 (CHAN_CONTROL)
01      00              flags = 0x00
02      00 00 00 4E     payload_length = 78 (network byte order)
06      7B 22 74 79 ... payload (78 bytes of UTF\-8 JSON)
.EE
.SH Binary frame: EVAL command on CHAN_COMMAND
JSON payload:
\f[CR]{\(dqtype\(dq:\(dqeval\(dq,\(dqcommand\(dq:\(dqecho hello\(dq}\f[R]
.PP
Assuming the payload is 37 bytes:
.IP
.EX
Offset  Hex
00      01              channel = 1 (CHAN_COMMAND)
01      00              flags = 0x00
02      00 00 00 25     payload_length = 37
06      7B 22 74 79 ... payload (37 bytes of UTF\-8 JSON)
.EE
.SH Multi\-frame message
A large stdout response split across two frames:
.PP
Frame 1 (continued):
.IP
.EX
01 04 00 10 00 00  ...payload (1 MB)...
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
channel=1, flags=0x04 (CONTINUED), length=1048576
.PP
Frame 2 (final):
.IP
.EX
01 08 00 00 01 00  ...payload (256 bytes)...
.EE
.IP \(bu 2
channel=1, flags=0x08 (FINAL), length=256
